(# TensorPoW: A Tensor-Native Proof-of-Work Currency) Tj
T*
(Author: Arav Jain \(@aravhawk\)) Tj
T*
(Draft date: 2026-05-27) Tj
T*
(## Abstract) Tj
T*
(TensorPoW is a permissionless proof-of-work currency whose work function is) Tj
T*
(deterministic signed INT8 matrix multiplication with INT32 accumulation. The) Tj
T*
(chain separates high-rate transaction carriers, called fruits, from lower-rate) Tj
T*
(ordering checkpoints, called anchors. Fruits carry transactions under a) Tj
T*
(permanent work target. Anchors commit fruit sets, parent candidates, shard-tree) Tj
T*
(state, and fee-floor state under a WTEMA-adjusted target. The ledger is a pure) Tj
T*
(UTXO system: balances are derived only from unspent outputs, and genesis creates) Tj
T*
(no spendable allocation.) Tj
T*
(The design goal is to make useful parallel tensor hardware the natural mining) Tj
T*
(substrate while keeping consensus byte-exact across CUDA, MPS, x86 CPU, and ARM) Tj
T*
(CPU implementations. All consensus hashes use BLAKE3 with explicit domain) Tj
T*
(separation, all consensus integers are little-endian, and every consensus object) Tj
T*
(has a canonical byte encoding.) Tj
T*
(## 1. Introduction) Tj
T*
(Bitcoin demonstrated that an open network can order payments by making history) Tj
T*
(expensive to rewrite. TensorPoW keeps that central idea but changes the work) Tj
T*
(primitive and the block structure. Modern compute supply is increasingly shaped) Tj
T*
(by tensor accelerators. TensorPoW therefore uses a fixed 1024 by 1024 signed) Tj
T*
(INT8 matrix multiplication as its proof-of-work kernel. The output is serialized) Tj
T*
(as signed little-endian INT32 cells and hashed with BLAKE3.) Tj
T*
(TensorPoW is also a BlockDAG rather than a single-parent chain. Fruits can) Tj
T*
(reference multiple recent parents so honest work produced during propagation) Tj
T*
(races remains useful. Anchors periodically commit ordered fruit sets and the) Tj
T*
(state needed by wallets, miners, and light clients. The currency unit is TSC;) Tj
T*
(the atomic subunit is the matom, with 100,000,000 matoms per TSC.) Tj
T*
(This paper describes the permanent protocol semantics. It does not introduce a) Tj
T*
(numbered-generation network. Future incompatible rule changes require planned) Tj
T*
(hardforks of the same chain.) Tj
T*
(## 2. System Model) Tj
T*
(Nodes communicate over libp2p using TCP and QUIC transports, Noise security,) Tj
T*
(yamux multiplexing, Kademlia peer discovery, and Gossipsub 2.0 topic gossip.) Tj
T*
(The protocol defines gossip topics for fruits, anchors, and shard transactions.) Tj
T*
(Every wire message begins with the TensorPoW wire magic, a typed payload length,) Tj
T*
(the canonical payload, and a short BLAKE3-derived checksum. A malformed network) Tj
T*
(message is dropped before its payload can affect consensus.) Tj
T*
(The ledger is a pure UTXO ledger. There are no accounts, account nonces, smart) Tj
T*
(contract storage slots, or shared mutable balances. A transaction consumes) Tj
T*
(existing outpoints and creates new outputs. A transaction is valid only when the) Tj
T*
(referenced outputs exist, are unspent, satisfy their script templates, and obey) Tj
T*
(the active shard fee floor.) Tj
T*
(The network assumes asynchronous propagation and adversarial peers. It does not) Tj
T*
(enforce a consensus bandwidth minimum. Public routing is expected to work best) Tj
T*
(for operators that provision at least the recommended 10 MB/s bandwidth.) Tj
T*
(## 3. Cryptographic Commitments) Tj
T*
(Every consensus hash is BLAKE3 with a 32-byte output unless the protocol) Tj
T*
(explicitly calls for BLAKE3 XOF. Hash preimages begin with a one-byte domain) Tj
T*
(constant followed by canonical bytes. Domain separation is used for PoW) Tj
T*
(challenges, PoW outputs, fruit headers, anchor headers, transaction IDs,) Tj
T*
(signature hashes, outpoints, UTXO values, Merkle nodes, addresses, genesis,) Tj
T*
(shard trees, fee floors, and data-availability samples.) Tj
T*
(Ed25519 is the only active signature type at genesis. Transaction inputs carry a) Tj
T*
(signature type, and verifiers dispatch through a fixed signature table. Unknown) Tj
T*
(signature types fail validation. The reserved post-quantum signature identifier) Tj
T*
(does not validate until a hardfork activates rules for it.) Tj
T*
(Tensorcoin addresses are lowercase Bech32m strings with the human-readable part) Tj
T*
(`tsc`. The payload is `BLAKE3\(DOMAIN_ADDRESS || ed25519_public_key\)`, converted) Tj
T*
(from 8-bit bytes to 5-bit Bech32m words. Mixed case, wrong HRP, invalid) Tj
T*
(checksums, invalid padding, and wrong decoded payload lengths are invalid.) Tj
T*
(## 4. Tensor Proof of Work) Tj
T*
(The PoW kernel is:) Tj
T*
(```text) Tj
T*
(C[row, col] = sum\(A[row, k] * B[k, col]\) for k in [0, 1024\)) Tj
T*
(```) Tj
T*
(`A` and `B` are signed INT8 matrices. `C` is a signed INT32 matrix. The) Tj
T*
(accumulator must not wrap, and floating-point promotion is not a valid) Tj
T*
(consensus implementation. Canonical output bytes serialize every INT32 cell in) Tj
T*
